; 128K: call the routine DE in the music bank
;
; Pushes the address of #R$85BE (page bank 0 back in) and then DE, and falls into #R$85C7, which pages the music bank in
; and RETs: the RET jumps to DE, and the RET at the end of that routine returns to #R$85BE, which restores bank 0 and
; returns to the caller of this routine. HL and the other registers reach the music routine unchanged, except BC.
; .
; Hardware: writes the paging port $7FFD (through #R$85CA).
;
; DE Address of the routine in the music bank ($C000-$FFFF)
; HL Argument passed on to that routine (module address, see #R$85E8)
; O:BC Changed
@label=CallInMusicBank
@isub=LD BC,PageInBank0
c$85C2 LD BC,$85BE          ; return address of the music routine
 $85C5 PUSH BC
 $85C6 PUSH DE              ; the RET at $85D4 jumps here
@label=PageInMusicBank
*$85C7 LD A,($8506)         ; port value that selects the music bank (#R$8506)
